    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, I guess I'm here because... things at work have been really intense lately. I'm a buyer, and I just can't shake this feeling that people at the office, and even some of our vendors, are tracking my buys. Which is wild because vendors are supposed to be professional, right? Like this one guy we deal with, he sells us these imported ceramic mugs, and he always wears these incredibly flashy ties. Last week it was bright yellow with little golf clubs on it. I don't even know who plays golf anymore, honestly. My uncle used to play golf all the time, but he messed up his shoulder slipping on some ice a few years ago. It was a whole ordeal, he had to get surgery and everything, and his physical therapist was just awful to him. \n\nBut... wait, what was I saying? Oh, right, the vendors. Yeah, they're tracking me and messing with the launch numbers just to make me look stupid. My supervisor keeps pulling up the reports and showing me that the data doesn't prove that they're doing it, but I just know they are. It's really getting to me, so... yeah, that's what really made me come in.",
