    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been feeling that people at work and the vendors are tracking you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's been going on for a while. I'd say roughly ten months now. Ten months of just... knowing they're watching me. And the voice, too, that started around the same time. It's been ten months of that. Which is funny, because ten months ago was right around the time I bought my new car. It's a Honda Civic, silver. I really wanted the blue one, but the dealership didn't have it in stock, and the salesman was incredibly pushy. He kept trying to upsell me on this undercoating package that I know is just a scam. My dad always told me never to buy the undercoating. He was a mechanic for thirty years, worked at this little shop downtown that used to be a gas station in the fifties. They still had the old pumps out front, just for show, you know? Anyway, the salesman was wearing this terrible cologne, smelled like pine needles and cheap aftershave... but yeah, about ten months.",
