    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past ten months, have you had times where you felt unusually energized, high, or wired, needing much less sleep than usual?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, definitely. I get these stretches where I feel just... electric. Like the whole city is opening up for me, you know? Like I can do anything. Actually, speaking of the city, they just started tearing up the pavement on 5th Avenue right by my apartment, and it's a total mess. The jackhammers start at like 6 AM. The guys running them always wear those neon green vests, which reminds me of this crossing guard we had in elementary school. Mr. Henderson. He used to give out butterscotch candies, but only if you looked both ways twice. I don't even like butterscotch, it's too sweet, it always gets stuck in your teeth... but anyway, what were we talking about? \n\nRight, being wired. Yeah, I get super energized like that. But then the problem is, if someone at the office questions a purchase order I made, or if my supervisor tells me to slow down, I just explode. I snap way harder than I mean to. Like, I yelled at our shipping guy the other day just for using the clear packing tape instead of the brown paper kind. Which really does mess up the recycling process, but still, I probably shouldn't have yelled.",
