    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you still hear the voice or feel like you're being tracked during times when you aren't feeling energized or wired?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, definitely. Even when I have those calmer stretches... like, there was a time recently where I was actually sleeping normally again, not feeling like I was running the whole market or totally wired. But I still spent a few weeks fully believing people were tracking my buys. And I was still hearing that voice when I was back in the stockroom. Which is super annoying because the stockroom is where we keep all the overflow for the seasonal stuff. Right now it's just packed with these cheap plastic Halloween decorations. They smell awful, like that weird factory chemical smell? It reminds me of this factory tour I went on in high school. We went to a place that made rubber boots. The smell was so strong I actually got a headache, and the bus ride back was terrible because the suspension on the school bus was completely shot. Every pothole felt like we were crashing. My friend Tyler was sitting next to me, and he had brought this giant bag of salt and vinegar chips, which just made my stomach turn even more... \n\nBut wait, what was the question? Oh, right, the voice and the tracking. Yeah, even when I'm not feeling all electric and I'm sleeping fine, that stuff doesn't go away. It was still happening for a few weeks during that calm period.",
